From: dtrace.nix maintainers
Subject: module,fbt: avoid eager kallsyms walks

The kernel's /proc/kallsyms iterator is extremely expensive under emulation,
especially for modern kernels with Rust symbols.  Most DTrace operations do
not need address-bearing kernel symbols: fprobes are enumerated by tracefs and
typed by BTF.  Bootstrap the vmlinux BTF module cheaply, enumerate FBT probes
from the kernel's canonical available-filter-functions list, and load the full
symbol table only for explicit name/address symbol resolution.

